Notes on the tricky parts: `divmod` on a possibly negative month index does the right thing in Python (floor division), so backward shifts across year boundaries fall out for free; and since `day` is taken from the *original* input rather than the running result, clamping never sticks (2024-01-31 + 1 + 1 is 2024-03-31, not 2024-03-29).

