Requirements & edge cases (worked through first):

- 5 fields, ranges: min 0-59, hour 0-23, dom 1-31, month 1-12, dow 0-6 (7 must fail).
- Item grammar: `*`, `n`, `a-b` (a≤b), each optionally `+ /n` (n≥1). `*/n` → from field min; `a-b/n` → from a to b; `a/n` → from a to field max; bare `n` → just that value.
- Reject: wrong field count, empty field/item, `0` step, non-digits, out-of-range values, reversed ranges, multiple slashes/hyphens.
- Day logic: restricted = field string is not exactly `*`. Both restricted → OR; one → that one; neither → every day.
- `after` has minute precision, so "strictly later" = strictly greater (hour, minute) on the same day, or any allowed time on later days.
- Search bounded to `after + 5 years` (Feb-29 floor); no hit → `ValueError`.
- dow mapping: Python `weekday()` Mon=0 → cron `(weekday()+1)%7`, Sunday=0.

