"""Arithmetic expression evaluator: ``evaluate(expr) -> int | float``.

Grammar (recursive descent, lowest precedence first)::

    expression := term (('+' | '-') term)*
    term       := unary (('*' | '/') unary)*
    unary      := '-' unary | power
    power      := atom ('^' unary)?            # right-associative
    atom       := NUMBER | '(' expression ')'

Unary minus lives between ``term`` and ``power``, so it binds *looser* than
``^`` (``-2 ^ 2 == -4``) but tighter than ``*``/``/``, and it may be stacked
(``--3``).  The right-hand side of ``^`` is parsed with ``unary``, which makes
